# API Sync Rule

When changing a backend endpoint, update the frontend in the same change:

| Backend change | Frontend update |
|----------------|-----------------|
| New endpoint | Hook in `frontend/src/hooks/use*.ts` |
| Changed path/method | Matching `api.get/post/patch/delete` call |
| New enum value | Label in `frontend/src/lib/constants.ts` |
| New query params | Hook filters + page filter UI |
| Changed response shape | Components consuming the hook |

## Ticket endpoints → `useTickets.ts`

All ticket mutations live in `useTicketAction(id)` — add new actions there, not inline in pages.

## Checklist

```
- [ ] Controller method matches hook call (path + method + body)
- [ ] Arabic toast message on success/error
- [ ] queryClient.invalidateQueries for affected keys
- [ ] Role-gated button on page (if user-facing action)
- [ ] Swagger @ApiOperation updated
```

See skill: `barmijly-api-sync`
